You need to make your own. I personally would take another published pig brain paper, download their dataset, and re-create their main clustering figure as best as I could to use Garnett's automatic marker file compilation, and use this to train the classifier on my own data. I do not know how well cross-species classifiers work, or if Garnett will allow it at all. Considering there is only one db= argument, I doubt it. Refer to the tutorial for training.

